WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Instructor] We're
told a certain taco stand

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:06.940
sells t tacos per day
for a net profit of $300.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.660
Each taco costs c dollars to make,

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.160
and is sold for p dollars.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.510
Write an equation that
relates t, c, and p.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.310
So pause this video and
see if you can do that.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.870
All right, now let's work this together.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.120
So let's just remind ourselves
what's going on here.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.860
So we have the number of
tacos sold per day is t,

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.860
so t = number of tacos sold per day.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:41.460
They tell us the net profit of $300,

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.023
so we could say 300 = net profit.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:52.050
They tell us that each taco
costs c dollars to make,

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.130
so c = cost per taco.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.330
And then p is what each taco is sold for,

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:06.470
right over there, is sold for p dollars,

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:11.470
so p = the price per taco.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.770
So how do we figure out what
the net profit is going to be?

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.250
Well, we can write it this way.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.920
Net profit is going to be equal to

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.790
the total amount of
money that you bring in

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.680
minus the total amount of
money that you have to spend.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.920
So what is going to be the
total amount that you bring in?

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.800
Well it's gonna be the
amount you sell times...

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.970
Well it's gonna be the
number of tacos you sell

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:37.160
times the price per taco.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.920
So t X p, this is how much
money you're bringing in,

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.010
but of course you have to
also subtract out your costs.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.160
Well, what's going to be your cost?

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.680
It's going to be the number of tacos

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.870
times the cost per taco.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.500
That's how much we're going to spend.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.500
So the number of tacos
times the cost per taco.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.960
Now here I've written
everything as variables.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.610
Well, I wrote net profit out,

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.920
but they told us that net
profit is equal to 300.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.490
So I could write it like this.

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:11.490
300 = t X p, I'll do it
with those same colors,

00:02:12.328 --> 00:02:13.245
tp - tc.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.040
Now, it's completely possible

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.530
that they didn't give us
net profit as $300 per day,

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.600
and instead they said that
is one of the variables,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.970
and they gave one of the other variables,

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:30.970
and that would have been okay,

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.740
we could have used the same logic.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.500
Whatever they didn't give
us we could've set up

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.320
as a variable of whatever
they did give us,

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.880
maybe they gave us the price per taco,

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.460
we could've put that as a given number.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.170
Now, I know what some
of y'all are thinking.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:44.410
You didn't get exactly this.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.360
You might've thought
about it the other way.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.870
You might've thought about it as

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.670
the profit is going to be equal to

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:55.140
the number of tacos times
the profit per taco.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.360
And what's going to be
the profit per taco?

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.400
Well, that's going to be how
much each taco is sold for

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:04.340
minus how much each taco costs.

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.780
And this also would have
been completely credible.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.810
And if you look at these two,

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.280
they're actually algebraically equivalent.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.210
If you factor out t here,

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.873
you get this expression on the right.

